# 0008. CI lints in an Arch container, including the greeter's Hyprland config

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

Every PR runs `make lint` in an Arch container, because a broken `system/hyprland.lua` means no login
screen at boot and none of it can be checked on the Mac.

## Technical details
- **`make lint`**: `config/config.json` parses; shellcheck on the launcher, `display-manager.sh`,
  `diagnose.sh`, `list-sessions.sh`; `Hyprland --verify-config --config system/hyprland.lua` (must
  say `config ok`); qmllint from `/usr/lib/qt6/bin`, informational (mostly false "not found on type"
  warnings for Quickshell singletons).
- **CI**: GitHub Actions in `archlinux:base`, as a non-root user (Hyprland refuses root), same as
  `archminimal-hypr` ADR 0010.
- **Limits**: CI proves the files parse; anything in the login flow needs a real login on the VM
  before merging.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: GitHub Actions, archlinux:base, Hyprland, Quickshell, shellcheck.
